WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.280
I hear from lots of
people every day

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:06.840
who are concerned about how
their diet is affecting their health.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.560
They need answers
based on facts.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:10.480
In other words,

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.480
in the peer-reviewed
medical literature,

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:15.360
and that is what
I’m here for.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.560
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.080
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:23.640
Today we have the second
in a two part series

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.160
where I offer some highlights from
my latest book, How Not to Age,

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.560
taped in front of
a live audience.

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.320
We pick up our
story with tips

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:35.840
on how to keep our vital organs
in good working order.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:40.480
What can we do to protect our
bones, bowels, bladder, and circulation?

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:43.240
Our hair, hearing,
and hormone balance?

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:45.280
Immune function,
joint health?

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:46.240
Our minds and our muscles?

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:47.280
Sex life and skin?

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.440
Our teeth, vision, and finally,
our dignity in death.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:54.880
Let me just share
a few quick pearls.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:55.920
For example,

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:03.880
did you know that 85 percent
of bone-related fracture risk

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:08.000
has nothing to do with
your bone mineral density?

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.440
That’s just been drilled
into our heads by big pharma

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.480
and a billion-dollar bone
density screening industry.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:20.440
Fractures are primarily due
to falling, not osteoporosis.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:24.200
So, it’s the age-related muscle
loss and impaired balance

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.960
that may be breaking
most of our bones—

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:27.720
which is good news,

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.120
because there’s something
we can do something about it.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:31.669
Seven randomized
controlled trials

00:01:31.669 --> 00:01:32.480
found that strength
and balance training

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.480
can cut fracture
rates nearly in half—

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:35.760
and that’s just
during the trial.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:39.520
In the five years after this
one-year study ended,

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:42.520
those who had previously
been randomized

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.760
to the combined strength
and balance group,

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:48.280
suffered 74 percent
fewer fractures.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:54.760
That’s far more effective than
osteoporosis drugs like Fosamax

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:58.800
that can cause fractures—
atypical femoral fractures,

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:01.000
in as many as
1 in 300 users.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.400
They are called “atypical,”

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.080
because they occur
not after a fall or trauma

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:08.920
but just during routine
activities, like walking,

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:12.440
twisting at the hip,
or even just standing still.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:18.520
Thanks to the drug,
your femur, your thigh bone,

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:26.000
the biggest bone in your body—
just cracks in half.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:31.559
Too cruel an irony from a drug
that’s supposed to protect your bones.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:32.400
After bones,

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.400
I talk about preserving
your bowel function

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:39.280
in chapter number two.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:42.120
Randomize constipated
diabetics

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:45.080
to either cookies containing
a tablespoon (20 g) a day

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:45.960
of ground flaxseeds

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:48.880
or flax-free placebo
cookies for 12 weeks

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:52.880
and not only does the flax
improve constipation symptoms

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:56.000
but resulted in an eight-pound
weight loss over placebo,

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.080
25-point lower
blood sugars,

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:03.080
an astounding drop in hemoglobin A1c,
and 17-point lower LDL cholesterol.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:07.000
All for about 10 cents a day
of ground flaxseeds.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.120
For a head-to-head test
between flaxseeds and psyllium,

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.480
sold as Metamucil,

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:15.120
a third cookie group was added
with 10 grams of psyllium,

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:19.560
and the flaxseed beat out the
psyllium for constipation relief,

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:22.840
weight, blood sugars,
and cholesterol—

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:26.040
and, is about four
times cheaper.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:30.920
Flaxseeds were also directly compared
to the prescription laxative lactulose

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:35.440
and worked better as well.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:36.660
Bladder function!

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:40.720
The prevalence of overactive
bladder syndrome increases with age,

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.920
reaching about
one in three.

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:48.760
No wonder bladder-relaxing drugs
are a multibillion-dollar industry,

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:50.920
yet may only reduce
bathroom breaks

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:55.640
by a half a pee a day
compared to placebo.

00:03:55.640 --> 00:04:00.560
But a quarter teaspoon (500 mg) a day
of dried cranberry powder

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:02.680
worked nearly
four times better,

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:06.240
about two fewer daily trips
to the bathroom over placebo,

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.880
and that’s without any of
the drug’s side effects:

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:11.160
dry mouth, constipation,
sedation, impaired cognition,

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:12.480
rapid heartbeat,
urinary retention,

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:15.640
and the visual disturbances
that lead almost two-thirds

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.320
to stop taking the drugs,

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:24.160
whereas cranberries
are just tangy.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:27.600
Urinary incontinence is a common
problem among older adults,

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.600
particularly women,
thanks to childbirth.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:36.120
Systemic menopausal hormone therapy
like Premarin actually makes it worse,

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:39.320
but local, vaginal
estrogen may help.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:43.200
What works five times better
than estrogen cream though?

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:47.200
Kegel exercises,
pelvic floor exercises,

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:59.840
as I detail in the section
“Jacked in the Box.”

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:04.640
For men, urinary issues are more
an enlarged prostate problem,

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:08.760
having to get up
multiple times at night,

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:13.800
wee hours of the night.

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:19.800
Cranberries to the
rescue there again.

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:23.520
Even just an eighth of a teaspoon (250 mg)
a day of powdered cranberries

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:26.520
can significantly improve
prostate symptoms.

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:29.000
You can buy cranberry
powder in bulk

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:33.000
at a cost of less than
a penny per day.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.040
What about
saw palmetto,

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:38.760
the most common herbal supplement
used for prostate symptoms?

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:41.480
Based on dozens of randomized,
controlled trials

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:46.440
involving nearly 5,000 men:
no clinical benefits.

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:49.480
But pumpkin seeds work.

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:52.560
More than a thousand men with
prostate symptoms were randomized

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:56.720
to either about a tablespoon (15 g) a day
of plain pumpkin seed kernels,

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:59.480
a proprietary pumpkin seed
extract, or a placebo.

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:05.440
The study was funded by the drug
company that made the supplement,

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:09.760
but the supplement
totally flopped,

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:14.080
while the pumpkin seeds
themselves worked.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:20.240
Pumpkin seed oil was pitted against
the leading drug for hair loss in women.

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:25.120
A little less than a quarter teaspoon (1 ml)
applied to the scalp once a day

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:30.600
versus a dose of the drug,
and they both worked,

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:33.400
but the drug worked better.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:38.120
Rosemary oil, however,
may be more closely matched.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:42.320
A hundred balding men were randomized
to twice a day minoxidil like Rogaine

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:43.680
versus a rosemary lotion.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:44.680
It took six months,

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:49.120
but significant comparable improvement
in hair counts in both groups,

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:51.320
with no significant difference
between the two.

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:55.120
The rosemary lotion appeared
to work as well as the drug.

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:58.320
If you want to
give it a DIY try,

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:02.280
you can premix about 10 drops
of rosemary essential oil

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:04.800
to each fluid ounce (30 ml)
of your favorite lotion

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:09.280
and rub a quarter teaspoon (1.23 ml)
into your scalp twice a day.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:12.240
Cost-wise,
that much rosemary oil

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:16.640
would come out to be
about a penny per week.

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:20.600
Let’s move on from hair
highlights to hormones.

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:23.440
I touched upon how
menopausal hormone therapy

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:29.520
can increase the risk of urinary
incontinence, but that’s not all.

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:32.480
If a thousand
postmenopausal women

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:35.680
take the standard hormone
regimen for ten years,

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:41.280
you’d not only expect 876
extra cases of urinary incontinence

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:43.640
that they would not
have got otherwise,

00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:48.560
but nine more cases of
invasive breast cancer,

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:50.160
eight more cases
of heart disease,

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:52.320
probably 22 more
cases of dementia,

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:54.520
21 more cases of
gallbladder disease,

00:07:54.520 --> 00:07:57.280
nine more strokes,
and 21 more blood clots—

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:03.440
though not a single
partridge nor pear tree.

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:06.200
However, hormone
therapy is highly effective

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:08.400
in decreasing
menopausal hot flashes.

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:12.640
Is there any way to keep cool
without the clots and cancer?

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:17.360
In the U.S., menopausal hot
flashes are considered inevitable,

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:24.200
but there isn’t even a word
for hot flash in Japanese.

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:28.600
This may be due to their
greater consumption of soy foods,

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:32.160
but you don’t really know
until you put it to the test.

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:33.920
Harvard’s Center of Excellence
in Women’s Health

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:36.800
funded a randomized,
crossover trial

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:39.640
of a half a cup (118 ml) of
unsalted soy nuts a day

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:45.400
and achieved about a 40 to 45
percent reduction in hot flashes

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:48.720
within two weeks compared
to the control group.

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:53.640
Given that a plant-based
diet may also be effective

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:56.320
for managing
menopausal symptoms,

00:08:56.320 --> 00:09:05.440
researchers decided to combine the two:
a plant-based diet plus whole soybeans.

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:12.080
In fact, two randomized controlled trials
found that plant-based nutrition

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:15.160
with a daily half cup (86 g) of
cooked whole soybeans

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:19.520
can reduce the number of serious
hot flashes by 84 to 88 percent

00:09:19.520 --> 00:09:21.160
within twelve weeks.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:24.280
Overall, most randomized to
the plant-based bean group

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:26.480
ended up free of
moderate-to-severe hot flashes

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:32.040
compared to about 95 percent
still suffering in the control group.

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:33.320
Lots of other
things can help.

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:34.840
Whole fennel seeds,

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.440
powdered into capsules
to pit them against placebo

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:40.480
in a double-blind trial significantly
improved menopausal symptoms

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:42.880
at a dose of just
a teaspoon (2 g) a day.

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:47.920
Fenugreek may also help at a dose
of one and a half teaspoons (6 g) a day,

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:52.720
though not as much as hormones,
but without the side effects.

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:58.360
Though fenugreek can make your
pee smell like maple syrup,

00:09:58.360 --> 00:09:59.120
sounds like a bonus!

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:06.800
The nice thing about
studying spices

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:10.040
is that entire servings
can be stuffed into a pill,

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:12.120
to pit them
against placebo.

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:15.200
A quarter teaspoon (1 g) of
black cumin powder a day

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:17.720
led to significant
improvements in memory

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:23.520
and other tests of cognition within
nine weeks compared to placebo.

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:25.800
Black sesame seeds—

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:30.040
less than a teaspoon (2.52 g) a day
of ground black sesame seeds—

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:32.360
stuffed into capsules
against placebo,

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:36.680
drove down systolic blood pressures
by eight points within a month.

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:43.080
If sustained, that alone could decrease
the risk of stroke by about a quarter.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:45.800
What else can we powder?
Strawberries!

00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:47.840
Osteoarthritis patients
were randomized

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:50.560
to two ounces (50 g) of freeze-
dried strawberry powder

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:54.960
versus a fake, strawberry-flavored
and colored placebo powder,

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:57.400
and, compared to placebo,

00:10:57.400 --> 00:11:01.960
the real strawberries signiﬁcantly
decreased constant pain,

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:04.520
intermittent pain,
and total knee pain,

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:09.000
and improved disability
and overall quality of life.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:14.760
Osteoarthritis is the most frequent cause
of physical disability among older adults,

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:16.320
yet how do we treat it?

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:21.480
Acetaminophen—Tylenol is
considered the first-line pain killer,

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:25.080
but guess what:
it doesn’t work.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:25.960
I mean—it works,

00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:28.720
just not much better
than a sugar pill,

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:33.680
but at least it’s not going
to make matters worse,

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:37.760
like other things we doctors have
cooked up, like steroid injections,

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:41.400
which actively worsen
joint deterioration

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:44.720
and offer no greater
pain relief than placebos.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:46.680
Or arthroscopic surgery,

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:48.640
which may end up
tripling our risk

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:52.200
of ending up having to get
a total full knee replacement.

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:56.960
I mean so, even if the strawberry
study is some total fluke,

00:11:56.960 --> 00:12:00.920
what’s the worst that can
happen, tastier smoothies?

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:05.360
And less than a quarter of a teaspoon
(~1.25 ml) of ground ginger a day

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:08.440
can beat out placebo
for joint pain.

00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:13.360
Researchers conclude
ginger, "therefore,

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:18.680
is recommended as a safe
drug for these patients,”

00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:24.440
but by “drug” they just mean
a couple pinches of the ground ginger

00:12:24.440 --> 00:12:27.640
you can buy
at any store.

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:31.120
There was even a
study on topical ginger—

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:35.160
at least, when applied
to the scrotum.

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:39.800
Paper-thin slices of ginger
applied over the inflamed testicles,

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:46.960
and the researchers
were, on the ball,

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:52.360
healing nearly three times
faster than the control group.

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:57.000
There have been more than a hundred
randomized, controlled trials on ginger,

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:59.960
shown to help with
nausea and vomiting

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:04.600
and everything from
COVID to PMS.

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:07.800
Heavy periods,
painful periods,

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:11.360
migraine headaches,
multiple sclerosis,

00:13:11.360 --> 00:13:13.080
and the list goes on.

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:18.640
Bottom line: “Mounting evidence suggests
ginger can promote healthy aging.”

00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:21.120
What about garlic?

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:28.160
Clinically proven to protect against
those who vant to suck your blood.

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:28.760
Literally.

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:32.560
A hundred marines were randomized
to a clove a day or placebo,

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:38.840
and those on garlic had
significantly fewer tick bites.

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:45.800
Though sadly, garlic does not appear
to help against other bloodsuckers.

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:48.440
So far, I’ve touched on
preserving your bones, bowels,

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:50.400
bladder, hair,
hormones, and joints,

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:56.320
but preserving your mind is
the largest chapter in the book,

00:13:56.320 --> 00:13:59.640
because dementia is one of our
most pressing public health problems

00:13:59.640 --> 00:14:04.560
and the most feared
condition of later life.

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:07.600
There’s a common misconception
that we have no control

00:14:07.600 --> 00:14:09.280
over whether we
develop dementia,

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:13.920
but the good news is that although
Alzheimer’s may be incurable,

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:18.800
at least it is preventable.

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:21.040
There is an
emerging consensus,

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:29.160
that “what is good for our hearts
is also good for our heads."

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:31.360
Clogged with cholesterol,
closing off our arteries—

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:34.120
clamping down
on blood flow.

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:38.400
What kind of brain arteries
do you want in your head?

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:43.800
Too much cholesterol in our blood is
unanimously recognized to be a risk factor

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:46.360
for the development of
Alzheimer’s disease.

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:49.400
Those with a total
cholesterol of 225 mg/dL or more

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:52.200
may have nearly
25 times the odds

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:57.200
of ending up with amyloid plaques
in their brain 10 to 15 years later.

00:14:57.200 --> 00:15:02.760
Cholesterol explains how the Alzheimer's
gene APOE4 ravages the brain.

00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:10.880
After all, APOE is the primary
cholesterol carrier in the brain.

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:16.640
LDL cholesterol in those with
bad gene variants of APOE

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:18.680
averages 40 points higher,

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:22.040
but switch people to a
diet lower in animal fat

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:25.400
and that cholesterol difference
can be effectively smoothed out.

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:28.600
So, diet can trump genetics.

00:15:29.560 --> 00:15:33.040
This may explain the
so-called Nigerian paradox,

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:37.560
where they have among the
highest rates of the Alzheimer's gene

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:42.680
but some of the lowest rates
of Alzheimer’s disease.

00:15:42.680 --> 00:15:43.760
How is that possible?

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:48.160
Genes load the gun,
but lifestyle pulls the trigger.

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:51.520
The paradox may be explained
by their low cholesterol levels,

00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:55.720
probably because of their
diets low in animal fat.

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:58.960
Human beings may
have evolved

00:15:58.960 --> 00:16:03.400
to maintain an LDL cholesterol
level of around 25 mg/dL,

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:10.160
but the average in the Western
world is approximately 120 mg/dL.

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:14.320
No wonder heart disease is
the leading cause of death

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:18.640
in high income countries,
and dementia is killer #2.

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:23.320
That helps explain why the
so-called Alzheimer’s gene

00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:27.320
is the single most important gene
when it comes to longevity, too.

00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:28.720
Which is good news,

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:32.920
because even if we’ve been
dealt some bad genetic cards,

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:37.280
we still may be able to
reshuffle the deck with diet.

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:41.640
So, in terms of dietary guidelines
for the prevention of Alzheimer’s,

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:45.760
we should center our diets
around vegetables, legumes,

00:16:45.760 --> 00:16:47.560
fruits, and whole grains.

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:51.880
In other words, the dietary
pillar of lifestyle medicine:

00:16:51.880 --> 00:16:54.520
whole food,
plant-based, nutrition.

00:16:54.520 --> 00:17:00.560
Or even simpler, plants,
plants, and more plants.

00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:02.560
Any plants in particular?

00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:06.920
Note that the directors of Loma Linda’s
Alzheimer’s Prevention Program

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:09.600
single out berries
and greens.

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:11.160
Eating strawberries
and spinach

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:14.480
can mitigate age-related
cognitive decline in rats,

00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:16.600
but what about in people?

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:21.240
When the cognition of hundreds
of twins was followed over a decade,

00:17:21.240 --> 00:17:24.800
consuming the berry pigments in less
than a quarter cup (23 g) of blueberries a day

00:17:24.800 --> 00:17:26.600
or about a daily
cup (138 g) of strawberries

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:31.840
was associated with slowed
cognitive aging by about four years,

00:17:31.840 --> 00:17:34.440
and nearly all of the randomized
controlled trials of blueberries

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:39.600
and cognitive performance found
improvements in at least one brain domain,

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:43.760
perhaps, because blueberry
consumption can improve blood flow

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:47.000
to certain critical
regions of the brain.

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:51.920
Now, the one study that flopped
mixed the berries with milk,

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:54.800
and we know the
addition of milk

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:57.520
prevents the artery
protective effects of tea

00:17:57.520 --> 00:18:00.560
and prevents the
bump in antioxidants

00:18:00.560 --> 00:18:03.160
that you’d normally get
eating dark chocolate

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:05.400
and impairs
the absorption

00:18:05.400 --> 00:18:09.040
of the autophagy-activating
compounds in coffee.

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:12.440
What about mixing
berries and cream?

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:16.625
The antioxidant activity of blueberries
is not just impaired by milk.

00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:21.680
Researchers found that the total
antioxidant capacity of our bloodstream

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:22.720
(measured in two
different ways)

00:18:22.720 --> 00:18:27.560
shoots up within an hour of eating
a cup-and-a-half (200 g) of blueberries with water

00:18:27.560 --> 00:18:30.360
and remains elevated
five hours later.

00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:34.960
With milk, maybe one
would expect less of a bump?

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:38.840
But in fact, they ended up even
worse than when they started.

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:41.040
After eating a whole
bowl of blueberries,

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:44.840
they ended up with less
antioxidant capacity in their body—

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:48.200
because they ate
blueberries with milk.

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:52.640
One reason greens may be referred
to as an anti-Alzheimer’s plant

00:18:52.640 --> 00:18:57.360
is because dark green leafy vegetables
can also improve blood flow in the brain

00:18:57.360 --> 00:18:58.720
in interventional trials.

00:18:58.720 --> 00:19:00.960
Randomize older adults
to the greens pigments

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:03.600
found in about a cup (12 mg) a
day’s worth of cooked kale

00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:07.720
and see significant improvements
in complex attention, cognitive flexibility.

00:19:07.720 --> 00:19:09.800
And those randomized
to even just a half cup

00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:13.400
of kale’s worth of the cruciferous
compound sulforaphane

00:19:13.400 --> 00:19:17.360
got significant improvements in
processing speed and working memory.

00:19:17.360 --> 00:19:21.200
Here’s the rate of cognitive
decline in elderly men and women

00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:24.440
eating a serving a
day of green leafies,

00:19:24.440 --> 00:19:28.240
compared to those only eating
greens about once every ten days.

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:31.760
Are you sitting down?

00:19:31.760 --> 00:19:33.760
“The rates of decline
among those

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:36.720
who consumed 1 to 2
servings of greens a day

00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:42.200
was the equivalent to
being 11 years younger… .”

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:47.880
So, now are you sitting
down to a big salad?

00:19:47.880 --> 00:19:50.040
Greens come up in
chapter after chapter.

00:19:50.040 --> 00:19:54.440
What’s the recommendation for preventing
age-related macular degeneration,

00:19:54.440 --> 00:19:57.360
our leading cause
of blindness?

00:19:57.360 --> 00:20:01.200
Or even treating it
in its earliest stages?

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:07.160
Consume a diet high
in green leafy vegetables.

00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:09.520
We’re talkin’ two to
three servings a day,

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:12.320
so at least greens at
every lunch and supper,

00:20:12.320 --> 00:20:15.880
with bonus points for sneaking them
into breakfast in, say, a green smoothie.

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:20.320
In fact, blending greens
can triple the bioavailability

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:24.360
of a key, vision-
protecting nutrient.

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:29.360
The main reason greens make
it into in my Anti-Aging 8 though,

00:20:29.360 --> 00:20:34.640
is because of the nitrates in
a serving or two of cooked greens

00:20:34.640 --> 00:20:38.800
can slow our metabolic
rate for the same reason,

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:43.200
a little shot of beet juice can help
free divers hold their breath longer,

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:46.940
because it improves the
efficiency of our mitochondria,

00:20:46.940 --> 00:20:49.320
the little power
plants in our cells,

00:20:49.320 --> 00:20:53.560
allowing us to effectively extract
more energy from each breath.

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:56.920
Another dietary intervention that has
a similar effect on slowing metabolism

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:58.320
is calorie restriction.

00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:02.160
The candle that burns half
as bright burns twice as long.

00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:08.560
But instead of starving all the time,
you can just eat a big salad.

00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:10.120
What else can
greens do?

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:11.960
In the Harvard Nurses’
Health Study,

00:21:11.960 --> 00:21:14.200
the consumption of leafy
greens appeared to protect

00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:16.520
against the
development of frailty,

00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:20.920
and when put to the test in a randomized,
double-blind, placebo-controlled trial,

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:23.400
the equivalent of two
thirds of a cup (158 ml) of spinach

00:21:23.400 --> 00:21:27.560
led to a significant boost in
muscle strength, muscle quality,

00:21:27.560 --> 00:21:30.440
and muscle mass in
older men and women.

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:33.680
A single cup (240 ml) of cooked greens
worth of vegetable nitrates

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:39.320
significantly boosted maximal power
and velocity in quads so much

00:21:39.320 --> 00:21:41.240
it was “functionally equivalent,

00:21:41.240 --> 00:21:46.640
to acutely reversing the effects
of several decades of aging.”

00:21:46.640 --> 00:21:50.960
A single cup (240 ml)
of cooked greens!

00:21:50.960 --> 00:21:54.440
Of course, when most people think
about maintaining muscle mass into old age,

00:21:54.440 --> 00:21:58.040
they don’t think spinach,
they think protein.

00:21:58.840 --> 00:22:04.080
But if you put together all of
the randomized, controlled trials

00:22:04.080 --> 00:22:09.560
of adding extra protein to the
diets of older men and women,

00:22:09.560 --> 00:22:17.480
you find no evidence that adding protein
increases muscle mass or strength.

00:22:17.480 --> 00:22:22.320
Yeah, but what if you have sarcopenia,
excessive age-related muscle loss?

00:22:22.320 --> 00:22:25.880
Surely then,
protein helps, right?

00:22:25.880 --> 00:22:26.760
No.

00:22:26.760 --> 00:22:29.520
No significant effect on physical
performance or muscle strength.

00:22:29.520 --> 00:22:32.280
What does work?
Exercise.

00:22:32.280 --> 00:22:34.160
When it comes to
age-related muscle loss,

00:22:34.160 --> 00:22:37.300
it’s use it or lose it.

00:22:37.300 --> 00:22:40.680
But maybe exercise
plus protein?

00:22:40.680 --> 00:22:41.520
No.

00:22:41.520 --> 00:22:44.680
Protein supplementation
does not significantly augment

00:22:44.680 --> 00:22:47.240
the effects of strength
training in older adults.

00:22:47.240 --> 00:22:54.640
In fact, one of my Anti-Aging 8
is protein restriction.

00:22:54.640 --> 00:23:03.040
Why do longevity experts like Valter Longo
recommend people cut down on protein

00:23:03.040 --> 00:23:05.160
to live longer?

00:23:05.160 --> 00:23:07.560
Here’s what Luigi Fontana
wrote in his book.

00:23:07.560 --> 00:23:11.120
He’s the director of another
leading longevity research center.

00:23:11.120 --> 00:23:14.680
Excess protein may
not mass your muscles,

00:23:14.680 --> 00:23:20.120
but it will accelerate aging.

00:23:20.120 --> 00:23:25.640
How do you boost the
pro-longevity hormone FGF21?

00:23:25.640 --> 00:23:27.880
Dietary protein restriction.

00:23:28.760 --> 00:23:33.640
How do you suppress the
age-accelerating enzyme IGF-1?

00:23:33.640 --> 00:23:36.720
You do it through dietary
protein restriction.

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:40.200
How do you suppress the
so-called motor of aging, mTOR?

00:23:40.200 --> 00:23:43.640
Dietary protein restriction.

00:23:43.640 --> 00:23:47.040
In fact, protein restriction was
the only intervention I could find

00:23:47.040 --> 00:23:50.960
that could slow down all
11 of the aging pathways,

00:23:50.960 --> 00:23:54.760
which is good news because
it’s easier to cut back on protein

00:23:54.760 --> 00:23:55.840
than it is to cut
back on everything

00:23:55.840 --> 00:23:57.880
and walk around
starving all the time.

00:23:58.520 --> 00:24:02.840
And, it may even
be easier than that.

00:24:02.840 --> 00:24:08.640
Most or all of the life-extending
benefits of protein restriction

00:24:08.640 --> 00:24:12.720
may be due to just restricting
particular amino acids like methionine.

00:24:12.720 --> 00:24:17.120
In that case, you could even
keep your protein intake the same

00:24:17.120 --> 00:24:19.120
but just swap sources,

00:24:19.120 --> 00:24:27.280
from animal proteins like meat
to plant-based sources like beans.

00:24:27.280 --> 00:24:29.520
So, in humans,

00:24:29.520 --> 00:24:34.440
methionine restriction can be achieved
using a predominately plant-based diet,

00:24:34.440 --> 00:24:40.640
which makes methionine restriction
feasible as a life-extension strategy.

00:24:40.640 --> 00:24:44.200
Of course, drug companies
look at this same data and think:

00:24:44.200 --> 00:24:52.000
What pharmaceuticals can we develop
to mimic these dietary interventions?

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:56.640
Anything else to maintain muscle mass
other than greens and machines?

00:24:56.640 --> 00:24:59.240
How about cocoa beans!

00:24:59.240 --> 00:25:02.160
Older men and women randomized
to a single tablespoon (22 g)

00:25:02.160 --> 00:25:04.200
of regular cocoa
powder a day

00:25:04.200 --> 00:25:06.880
experienced a significant
improvement in muscle strength,

00:25:06.880 --> 00:25:11.280
muscle mass, and all four
tests of physical performance.

00:25:11.280 --> 00:25:15.520
And no, the study was
not funded by Hershey’s.

00:25:15.520 --> 00:25:18.800
Unfortunately, the tastiest
cocoa doesn’t work as well.

00:25:18.800 --> 00:25:23.520
The control groups here were given
the same amount of highly Dutched cocoa—

00:25:23.520 --> 00:25:25.000
alkalized cocoa,

00:25:25.000 --> 00:25:28.000
where some of the bitter compounds
removed in the Dutching process

00:25:28.000 --> 00:25:31.840
are the very flavonoids
responsible for the benefits.

00:25:31.840 --> 00:25:34.640
But natural cocoa is so good

00:25:34.640 --> 00:25:38.440
it can improve walking performance
in those with peripheral artery disease,

00:25:38.440 --> 00:25:40.400
not only by
improving blood flow,

00:25:40.400 --> 00:25:42.160
but, as muscle
biopsies showed,

00:25:42.160 --> 00:25:44.920
by improving
mitochondrial activity.

00:25:44.920 --> 00:25:48.760
This is consistent with improved
mitochondrial structure

00:25:48.760 --> 00:25:51.720
as well in biopsies taken
from people’s quads.

00:25:51.720 --> 00:25:59.360
Though this study was
actually funded by Hershey’s.

00:25:59.360 --> 00:26:01.840
What else can cocoa do?

00:26:01.840 --> 00:26:04.880
Increase the circulation
within our skin,

00:26:04.880 --> 00:26:08.480
boosting it 70 percent
within two hours,

00:26:08.480 --> 00:26:10.080
after less than a tablespoon.

00:26:10.080 --> 00:26:12.800
Do that every day and
within three months,

00:26:12.800 --> 00:26:16.080
you end up with significantly
improved skin thickness,

00:26:16.080 --> 00:26:20.040
density, and hydration,
but no change in wrinkles.

00:26:20.040 --> 00:26:22.600
However, keep it
up for six months,

00:26:22.600 --> 00:26:25.280
and you do see an
improvement in wrinkles,

00:26:25.280 --> 00:26:27.720
a significant decrease
of wrinkle depth,

00:26:27.720 --> 00:26:31.520
along with an improvement in
skin elasticity within 12 weeks—

00:26:31.520 --> 00:26:35.040
all by making your life
a little more chocolatey,

00:26:35.040 --> 00:26:39.720
by just adding some natural
cocoa powder to your daily diet.

00:26:39.720 --> 00:26:44.120
I put it in my oatmeal with some
canned water-packed tart cherries

00:26:44.120 --> 00:26:48.240
for a chocolate-covered
cherry sensation.

00:26:48.240 --> 00:26:50.760
What else can we
do for our skin?

00:26:50.760 --> 00:26:52.920
Well, there certainly
are other antioxidant,

00:26:52.920 --> 00:26:55.720
anti-inflammatory,
glycotoxin-free foods;

00:26:55.720 --> 00:26:58.640
so, when patients
inquire about a diet

00:26:58.640 --> 00:27:01.720
that might contribute
to younger-looking skin,

00:27:01.720 --> 00:27:03.480
evidence supports
a recommendation

00:27:03.480 --> 00:27:05.960
to follow a whole food,
plant-based diet.

00:27:05.960 --> 00:27:12.880
But the most important thing to
prevent skin aging is avoid the sun.

00:27:12.880 --> 00:27:19.440
Exposure to sunlight may account
for 90 percent of visible skin aging.

00:27:19.440 --> 00:27:21.760
That’s why
dermatologists agree

00:27:21.760 --> 00:27:24.560
there’s nothing more important
to slow the signs of aging

00:27:24.560 --> 00:27:28.156
than to protect your
skin from the sun.

00:27:28.156 --> 00:27:31.160
So, the gold standard is considered
to be the use of sunscreens

00:27:31.160 --> 00:27:34.800
in the daytime and
“retinoids” at night.

00:27:34.800 --> 00:27:39.560
They’re talking about a prescription-
only form of topical vitamin-A,

00:27:39.560 --> 00:27:41.720
also known as
all-trans-retinoic-acid,

00:27:41.720 --> 00:27:44.680
or tretinoin
(sold as Retin-A),

00:27:44.680 --> 00:27:50.640
that has been widely proven
to improve skin appearance.

00:27:50.640 --> 00:27:57.080
The only problem is
that it may kill you.

00:27:57.080 --> 00:27:59.520
“Topical Tretinoin Therapy
and All-Cause Mortality”,

00:27:59.520 --> 00:28:02.280
a randomized controlled trial
had to be stopped early,

00:28:02.280 --> 00:28:05.960
because significantly more people
were dying in the retinoic acid group,

00:28:05.960 --> 00:28:07.960
compared to the
placebo-cream group.

00:28:07.960 --> 00:28:09.120
When applied topically,

00:28:09.120 --> 00:28:12.040
1 to 8 percent is absorbed
into the bloodstream.

00:28:12.040 --> 00:28:13.680
Could it be
killing people?

00:28:13.680 --> 00:28:15.280
While the debate
continues

00:28:15.280 --> 00:28:18.400
as to whether the increase in deaths
was just some statistical fluke

00:28:18.400 --> 00:28:20.240
or a real biological effect,

00:28:20.240 --> 00:28:26.200
tretinoin continues to be banned
in Europe for cosmetic purposes.

00:28:26.200 --> 00:28:30.120
So, what can we use?

00:28:30.120 --> 00:28:34.400
Topical niacinamide,
also known as nicotinamide,

00:28:34.400 --> 00:28:39.520
is described as one of the best-studied
anti-aging skin cream ingredients

00:28:39.520 --> 00:28:42.240
(which is not
saying much),

00:28:42.240 --> 00:28:45.520
but it has been shown
to reduce yellowing,

00:28:45.520 --> 00:28:49.960
wrinkling, blotchiness,
and dark spots in aging facial skin,

00:28:49.960 --> 00:28:54.840
for example, significantly reducing
crow’s feet wrinkles around the eyes.

00:28:54.840 --> 00:28:57.040
This was a
split-face study

00:28:57.040 --> 00:29:01.240
in which 64 percent of the
niacinamide-side eye wrinkles

00:29:01.240 --> 00:29:03.160
had moderate or
marked improvement,

00:29:03.160 --> 00:29:08.160
compared to zero percent
of the placebo-side eyes.

00:29:08.160 --> 00:29:13.680
Topical vitamin C also offers similar
improvements over placebo in wrinkles,

00:29:13.680 --> 00:29:16.600
sallowness, and
skin tone or firmness.

00:29:16.600 --> 00:29:19.520
Unfortunately, vitamin C
is unstable in creams,

00:29:19.520 --> 00:29:22.240
turning an unsightly
brown when it oxidizes,

00:29:22.240 --> 00:29:23.280
limiting its shelf life.

00:29:23.280 --> 00:29:25.420
So instead, what the
skin care industry does,

00:29:25.420 --> 00:29:26.840
the skin care industry,

00:29:26.840 --> 00:29:30.880
they use the stable
vitamin C esters or derivatives,

00:29:30.880 --> 00:29:34.680
but there’s no evidence that these
compounds have comparable effects,

00:29:34.680 --> 00:29:36.720
likely because they’re
poorly absorbed

00:29:37.320 --> 00:29:39.680
and only minimally convert
to the active form.

00:29:39.680 --> 00:29:42.160
But the good news is you
can make your own.

00:29:42.160 --> 00:29:48.960
The 10 percent solution used in the study
retails for a ridiculous $127 an ounce (30 ml),

00:29:48.960 --> 00:29:54.160
but you can make a DIY solution
more than two thousand times cheaper

00:29:54.160 --> 00:29:57.160
by simply buying
ascorbic acid in bulk

00:29:57.160 --> 00:29:59.760
and mixing three grams
into 30 grams of water,

00:29:59.760 --> 00:30:03.360
at a cost of about
a nickel per ounce (30 ml).

00:30:03.360 --> 00:30:05.400
Drip a few drops into
the palm of your hand

00:30:05.400 --> 00:30:07.960
and use your fingertips to
apply it over your face,

00:30:07.960 --> 00:30:09.080
neck, and upper chest daily.

00:30:09.080 --> 00:30:10.840
(Just don’t get
it in your eyes.)

00:30:10.840 --> 00:30:13.640
And look, you can do the
same thing with niacinamide,

00:30:13.640 --> 00:30:17.320
which can be even
more ridiculously priced.

00:30:17.320 --> 00:30:19.400
But you can buy
it in bulk as well,

00:30:19.400 --> 00:30:23.600
at a 5,000 percent discount.

00:30:23.600 --> 00:30:25.920
I can go on and on,
and the book certainly does,

00:30:25.920 --> 00:30:31.840
but let me close out by
going back to the basics.

00:30:31.840 --> 00:30:35.400
From the anti-aging journal
Rejuvenation Research:

00:30:35.400 --> 00:30:39.880
“Finally, a regimen to extend
human life expectancy.”

00:30:39.880 --> 00:30:43.960
Was it some exotic new stem
cell treatment or gene therapy?

00:30:43.960 --> 00:30:47.960
No, it was a reference
to this Harvard analysis.

00:30:47.960 --> 00:30:50.560
More than a hundred thousand men
and women were followed for decades,

00:30:50.560 --> 00:30:53.080
and even just a few
basic lifestyle behaviors

00:30:53.080 --> 00:31:00.280
appeared to translate into 12 to 14
extra years for the average 50-year-old.

00:31:00.280 --> 00:31:01.560
Even at age 50,

00:31:01.560 --> 00:31:05.320
you may be able to add an
extra dozen years to your lifespan.

00:31:05.320 --> 00:31:07.640
Even at age 70,

00:31:07.640 --> 00:31:11.240
there could still be about
ten extra years on the table.

00:31:11.240 --> 00:31:14.440
And if you clean up
your life before 50,

00:31:14.440 --> 00:31:17.320
nearly 18 years may
be up-for-grabs,

00:31:17.320 --> 00:31:19.720
based on simple
common-sense behaviors.

00:31:19.720 --> 00:31:21.600
That’s the kind
of life extension

00:31:21.600 --> 00:31:25.360
extrapolating from some
of these lab animal experiments,

00:31:25.360 --> 00:31:29.760
but after decades of research and
hundreds of millions of dollars later,

00:31:29.760 --> 00:31:34.720
efforts to translate those results
into humans have largely been in vain.

00:31:34.720 --> 00:31:38.080
Yet, here we are
with human data

00:31:38.080 --> 00:31:41.800
suggesting dramatic life
extension is available to all of us.

00:31:41.800 --> 00:31:43.880
Right here, right now.

00:31:43.880 --> 00:31:51.040
The trillion-dollar pill that anti-aging
biotech has been promising us is here,

00:31:51.040 --> 00:31:57.160
it just effectively has to be administered
in the produce aisle and the gym.

00:31:57.760 --> 00:32:02.560
Turning back the clock,
not with a drug or a DeLorean,

00:32:02.560 --> 00:32:05.800
but just by eating and
living more healthfully.

00:32:05.800 --> 00:32:11.040
A midlife shift between
the ages of 45 and 64

00:32:11.040 --> 00:32:15.600
to even the barest
of minimums,

00:32:15.600 --> 00:32:17.920
the barest of minimums.

00:32:17.920 --> 00:32:18.800
So, what are
we talking about?

00:32:18.800 --> 00:32:20.600
At least 5 servings of
fruits and vegetables a day,

00:32:20.600 --> 00:32:22.680
walking even just
20 minutes a day,

00:32:22.680 --> 00:32:23.760
maintaining a
healthy weight,

00:32:23.760 --> 00:32:24.640
and not smoking,

00:32:24.640 --> 00:32:27.720
can result in a substantial
reduction in mortality

00:32:27.720 --> 00:32:30.160
even in the immediate future.

00:32:30.160 --> 00:32:32.400
We’re talking a 40
percent lower risk of dying

00:32:32.400 --> 00:32:34.440
in the subsequent
four years.

00:32:34.440 --> 00:32:37.960
The researchers conclude that
making the necessary changes

00:32:37.960 --> 00:32:42.400
to adhere to a healthy lifestyle
is extremely worthwhile,

00:32:42.400 --> 00:32:46.000
and middle-age is
certainly not too late to act.

00:32:46.000 --> 00:32:50.583
You hold the power.

00:32:50.800 --> 00:32:53.080
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:32:53.080 --> 00:32:57.160
about reinventing your health
through evidence-based nutrition.

00:32:57.160 --> 00:33:00.280
Go to nutritionfacts.org/testimonials.

00:33:00.280 --> 00:33:05.040
We may share it on our social
media to help inspire others.

00:33:05.040 --> 00:33:08.920
To see any graphs, charts, graphics,
images, or studies mentioned here,

00:33:08.920 --> 00:33:12.120
go to the Nutrition Facts
Podcast landing page.

00:33:12.120 --> 00:33:14.760
There you’ll find all the
detailed information you need –

00:33:14.760 --> 00:33:19.080
plus, links to all of the sources
we cite for each of these topics.

00:33:19.080 --> 00:33:22.360
My latest book, “How Not to Age”
is out now,

00:33:22.360 --> 00:33:26.160
premiering at #2 on the
New York Times Best Sellers list.

00:33:26.160 --> 00:33:28.480
Check it out at your
local public library.

00:33:28.480 --> 00:33:30.320
Of course, all the proceeds
of the sales

00:33:30.320 --> 00:33:33.320
of all my books goes
directly to charity.

00:33:33.320 --> 00:33:36.600
NutritionFacts.org is a nonprofit,
science-based public service,

00:33:36.600 --> 00:33:38.800
where you can sign up
for free daily updates

00:33:38.800 --> 00:33:42.720
on the latest in nutrition research
with bite-sized videos and articles.

00:33:42.720 --> 00:33:45.400
Everything on the
website is free.

00:33:45.400 --> 00:33:47.680
There’s no ads, no
corporate sponsorships,

00:33:47.680 --> 00:33:48.500
no kickbacks.

00:33:48.500 --> 00:33:52.320
It’s strictly non-commercial.
I’m not selling anything.

00:33:52.320 --> 00:33:54.960
I just put it up as a public service,
as a labor of love,

00:33:54.960 --> 00:33:57.320
as a tribute to
my grandmother,

00:33:57.320 --> 00:34:02.319
whose own life was saved
with evidence-based nutrition.

